cadence-look is adapted for this project from MotionSites Web Builder, a Claude skill by MotionSites
(https://github.com/Motionsites-AI/claude-skill, commit faa30d5).

Taken under the MIT License (LICENSE in this folder, section 1 of the original licence):
- references/craft.md, references/spec-template.md and references/techniques/*.md, copied unchanged;
- the workflow in SKILL.md, rewritten for Cadence;
- references/review.md, adapted for the tool's screens;
- scripts/shoot.cjs, rewritten in Node from the original scripts/shoot.py.

Not taken: the original's example prompts (examples/) and media shelf (media/). They are (c) MotionSites
and are not MIT. Cadence cannot use them in any case, because it loads nothing from the network. To read
the examples, install the original plugin: /plugin marketplace add Motionsites-AI/claude-skill

Changed for Cadence:
- the output is the tool's one offline HTML file, or a self-contained sample page;
- there are no CDNs, no Google Fonts and no remote media;
- fonts and libraries are bundled in vendor/ with their licences;
- samples, tests and screenshots use synthetic data only;
- Light and Dark both have to work;
- the tool's own tests decide when a change is done;
- the original's sponsor block is left out.

references/hero-pack.md is this project's own: the design notes for the look the WFM team chose.
